{
  "id": "queue-kanji-keep-going-open-unit",
  "title": "Keep going: a backfill kanji is not drawn between the cards of a half-answered unit; each rebuild is the tail of the build before (C-28d)",
  "covers": [
    "queue.kanji_keep_going_open_unit"
  ],
  "narrative": [
    "The word 日 (card ...10) was graduated two days ago with Easy (review state, not due). The new deckless word 学校 (card ...20) was created before the kanji notes 学 (card ...30), 校 (card ...40) and 日 (card ...50), all new and deckless. 日 is a backfill kanji; nothing was introduced today. Every fetch is made with keep_going=true, so the keep-going build is served.",
    "Step 0: before the first turn the keep-going share test refuses 日 (2 * 1 > 0 + 0 + 1). The deckless turn draws the unit 学, 校, 学校 (3 drawn); then 日 passes (2 <= 0 + 3 + 1). Order: 学, 校, 学校, 日. until_stop is 4.",
    "Step 1 answers 学 Easy. Step 2: 学 is the last new card and the deckless source's next word requires it, so the share step draws nothing while that unit is open (QueueBuilder rule 4 'Share step', 'Not while a unit is open'): 校, 学校 first, then 日 (2 <= 1 + 2 + 1), the tail of step 0. Without that rule 日 would pass at once (2 <= 1 + 0 + 1) and come before 校. until_stop is 3.",
    "Step 3 answers 校 Easy. Step 4: the same again: 学校, then 日. until_stop is 2."
  ],
